IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 12 (MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS, ss 59 to 68).
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation. Section 60 is the Minister's power to exempt; the orders made under it are encoded in the sgba-i-exempt-* modules.

§ `59. Appeal to Minister`

-- src:4016 | 59.—(1) Any licensee, any provider of an online communication
-- src:4017 | service or any provider of an internet access service (as the case may
-- src:4018 | be) aggrieved by —
-- src:4020 | (a) any decision of the Authority in the exercise of any
-- src:4021 | discretion vested in it by or under this Act; or
-- src:4023 | (b) anything contained in any Code of Practice or direction
-- src:4024 | issued by the Authority,
-- src:4026 | may appeal to the Minister.
@ref s 59(1) (src:4016-4026)
GIVEN `the person is a licensee, a provider of an online communication service or a provider of an internet access service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Authority in the exercise of a discretion vested in it by or under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by anything contained in a Code of Practice or direction issued by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59(1) the person may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    `the person is a licensee, a provider of an online communication service or a provider of an internet access service`
    AND (`the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Authority in the exercise of a discretion vested in it by or under this Act` OR `the person is aggrieved by anything contained in a Code of Practice or direction issued by the Authority`)

-- src:4030 | (2) Unless otherwise provided, where an appeal is made under this
-- src:4031 | section, the decision, direction or other thing appealed against must
-- src:4032 | be complied with until the appeal is determined.
@ref s 59(2) (src:4030-4032)
GIVEN `an appeal is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(2) the decision, direction or other thing appealed against must be complied with` MEANS
    IF `an appeal is made` AND (NOT `provision is made to the contrary`) THEN JUST (NOT `the decision is determined`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4034 | (3) The Minister may determine an appeal under this section by
-- src:4035 | confirming, varying or reversing any decision or direction of the
-- src:4036 | Authority or by amending any Code of Practice.
@ref s 59(3) (src:4034-4036)
GIVEN `the appeal is made under section 59` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59(3) the Minister may confirm, vary or reverse a decision or direction of the Authority, or amend a Code of Practice` MEANS
    `the appeal is made under section 59`

-- src:4038 | (4) The decision of the Minister in any appeal is final.
@ref s 59(4) (src:4038)
GIVEN `the Minister has decided the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(4) the Minister's decision is final` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has decided the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4040 | (5) In relation to the Minister determining an appeal against any
-- src:4041 | online Code of Practice issued or any direction given by, or the
-- src:4042 | exercise of any discretion vested in, the Authority under Part 10A,
-- src:4043 | sections 45H, 45I, 45K, 45L(3) and (4) and 45N(1) apply as if the
-- src:4044 | reference to the Authority in any limit as to any online Code of
-- src:4045 | Practice issued or any direction given by, or the exercise of any
-- src:4046 | discretion under those respective sections, were a reference to the
-- src:4047 | Minister.
@ref s 59(5) (src:4040-4047)
GIVEN `the appeal is against an online Code of Practice, a direction, or the exercise of a discretion under Part 10A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(5) sections 45H, 45I, 45K, 45L(3) and (4) and 45N(1) apply as if the reference to the Authority in a limit were a reference to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is against an online Code of Practice, a direction, or the exercise of a discretion under Part 10A` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `60. Exemption`

-- src:4053 | 60. The Minister may, subject to any terms and conditions that the
-- src:4054 | Minister may impose, by order in the Gazette, exempt —
-- src:4056 | (a) any class or description of shares or interests in shares from
-- src:4057 | section 35 or 36 or both; and
@ref s 60(a) (src:4053-4057)
GIVEN `the Minister has made an order in the Gazette exempting the class or description of shares or interests in shares from section 35 or 36 or both` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(a) the class or description of shares or interests in shares is exempt from section 35 or 36 or both` MEANS
    `the Minister has made an order in the Gazette exempting the class or description of shares or interests in shares from section 35 or 36 or both`

-- src:4053 | 60. The Minister may, subject to any terms and conditions that the
-- src:4054 | Minister may impose, by order in the Gazette, exempt —
-- src:4062 | (b) any person or class of persons from all or any of the
-- src:4063 | provisions of this Act or any subsidiary legislation made
-- src:4064 | under this Act.
@ref s 60(b) (src:4053-4064)
GIVEN `the Minister has made an order in the Gazette exempting the person or class of persons from all or any provisions of this Act or its subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is within that order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(b) the person is exempt from the provision of this Act or its subsidiary legislation the order names` MEANS
    `the Minister has made an order in the Gazette exempting the person or class of persons from all or any provisions of this Act or its subsidiary legislation` AND `the person is within that order`

§ `61. Equipment of licensee not subject to distress, etc.`

-- src:4068 | 61.—(1) No equipment or related facility of a licensee used for
-- src:4069 | providing, transmitting or delivering licensable broadcasting services
-- src:4070 | shall be subject to distress or be liable to be taken under or pursuant to
-- src:4071 | an enforcement order under any process of a court in any bankruptcy
-- src:4072 | or insolvency proceedings by any person without the prior approval
-- src:4073 | of the Minister in writing.
@ref s 61(1) (src:4068-4073)
GIVEN `the equipment or related facility of a licensee is used for providing, transmitting or delivering licensable broadcasting services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has given prior written approval to its distress or taking under an enforcement order in bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the equipment or facility may be subject to distress or taken under the process of a court` MEANS
    (NOT `the equipment or related facility of a licensee is used for providing, transmitting or delivering licensable broadcasting services`) OR `the Minister has given prior written approval to its distress or taking under an enforcement order in bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings`

-- src:4077 | (2) This section does not apply to any class licensee.
@ref s 61(2) (src:4077)
GIVEN `the licensee is a class licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61(2) section 61 applies to the licensee` MEANS
    NOT `the licensee is a class licensee`

§ `62. International dealings of Authority`

-- src:4081 | 62. For the purposes of the conduct of any international broadcast
-- src:4082 | and subject to this Act, the Authority may enter into direct
-- src:4083 | communication, arrangement and agreement with the lawfully
-- src:4084 | constituted broadcasting authority of any country or with any duly
-- src:4085 | authorised international agency or organisation concerned with
-- src:4086 | broadcasting (as the case may be) for —
-- src:4088 | (a) the purpose of providing facilities, fixing rates, arranging
-- src:4089 | terms of payment or accounting;
-- src:4091 | (b) operational, engineering or administrative purposes; or
-- src:4093 | (c) any other purpose necessary to properly fulfil its functions
-- src:4094 | under this Act.
@ref s 62 (src:4081-4094)
GIVEN `it is for the conduct of an international broadcast, and subject to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for providing facilities, fixing rates, arranging terms of payment or accounting; for operational, engineering or administrative purposes; or for any other purpose necessary to properly fulfil the Authority's functions under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62 the Authority may enter into direct communication, arrangement and agreement with the lawfully constituted broadcasting authority of a country or a duly authorised international agency or organisation concerned with broadcasting` MEANS
    `it is for the conduct of an international broadcast, and subject to this Act` AND `it is for providing facilities, fixing rates, arranging terms of payment or accounting; for operational, engineering or administrative purposes; or for any other purpose necessary to properly fulfil the Authority's functions under this Act`

§ `63. Government's right to determine international relations`

-- src:4098 | 63.—(1) Nothing in section 62 is deemed to abrogate the right of
-- src:4099 | the Government at any time to determine its relations with any
-- src:4100 | country or with any international agency or organisation.
@ref s 63(1) (src:4098-4100)
GIVEN `section 62 has been used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) the Government's right at any time to determine its relations with any country or international agency or organisation is abrogated` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:4102 | (2) The Authority and each broadcasting licensee must so discharge
-- src:4103 | their responsibilities and conduct their business as to comply with and
-- src:4104 | fulfil all international agreements, conventions or undertakings
-- src:4105 | relating to broadcasting to which Singapore is a party.
@ref s 63(2) (src:4102-4105)
GIVEN `the Authority or the broadcasting licensee complies with and fulfils all international agreements, conventions or undertakings relating to broadcasting to which Singapore is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 63(2) the Authority or the licensee has discharged its responsibilities as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the Authority or the broadcasting licensee complies with and fulfils all international agreements, conventions or undertakings relating to broadcasting to which Singapore is a party`

§ `64. Service of documents`

-- src:4112 | 64.—(1) A document that is permitted or required by this Act to be
-- src:4113 | served on a person may be served as described in this section.
@ref s 64(1) (src:4112-4113)
GIVEN `the document is permitted or required by this Act to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(1) the document may be served as section 64 describes` MEANS
    `the document is permitted or required by this Act to be served on a person`

-- src:4115 | (2) A document permitted or required by this Act to be served on an
-- src:4116 | individual may be served —
-- src:4118 | (a) by giving it to the individual personally;
-- src:4120 | (b) by sending it by prepaid registered post to the address
-- src:4121 | specified by the individual for the service of documents or,
-- src:4122 | if no address is so specified, the individual’s residential
-- src:4123 | address or business address;
-- src:4125 | (c) by leaving it at the individual’s residential address with an
-- src:4126 | adult apparently resident there, or at the individual’s
-- src:4127 | business address with an adult apparently employed there;
-- src:4129 | (d) by affixing a copy of the document in a conspicuous place
-- src:4130 | at the individual’s residential address or business address;
-- src:4132 | (e) by sending it by fax to the fax number last known to the
-- src:4133 | person giving or serving the document as the fax number
-- src:4134 | for the service of documents on the individual; or
-- src:4136 | (f) by sending it by email to the individual’s last email
-- src:4137 | address.
-- src:4139 | (3) A document permitted or required by this Act to be served on a
-- src:4140 | partnership (other than a limited liability partnership) may be
-- src:4141 | served —
-- src:4143 | (a) by giving it to any partner or other similar officer of the
-- src:4144 | partnership;
-- src:4146 | (b) by leaving it at, or by sending it by prepaid registered post
-- src:4147 | to, the partnership’s business address;
-- src:4149 | (c) by sending it by fax to the fax number used at the
-- src:4150 | partnership’s business address; or
-- src:4152 | (d) by sending it by email to the partnership’s last email
-- src:4153 | address.
-- src:4158 | (4) A document permitted or required by this Act to be served on a
-- src:4159 | body corporate (including a limited liability partnership) or an
-- src:4160 | unincorporated association may be served —
-- src:4162 | (a) by giving it to the secretary or other similar officer of the
-- src:4163 | body corporate or unincorporated association, or the
-- src:4164 | limited liability partnership’s manager;
-- src:4166 | (b) by leaving it at, or by sending it by prepaid registered post
-- src:4167 | to, the body corporate’s or unincorporated association’s
-- src:4168 | registered office or principal office in Singapore;
-- src:4170 | (c) by sending it by fax to the fax number used at the body
-- src:4171 | corporate’s or unincorporated association’s registered
-- src:4172 | office or principal office in Singapore; or
-- src:4174 | (d) by sending it by email to the body corporate’s or
-- src:4175 | unincorporated association’s last email address.
-- src:4177 | (5) In addition, a document permitted or required by this Act to be
-- src:4178 | served on an individual, a partnership, a body corporate or an
-- src:4179 | unincorporated association may be served —
-- src:4181 | (a) by giving an electronic notice to the individual,
-- src:4182 | partnership, body corporate or unincorporated
-- src:4183 | association (called in this section an addressee) by the
-- src:4184 | addressee’s chosen means of notification, stating that the
-- src:4185 | document is available and how the addressee may use the
-- src:4186 | addressee’s chosen means of access to access the
-- src:4187 | document’s contents;
-- src:4189 | (b) where by the exercise of reasonable diligence, the name of
-- src:4190 | any individual or a body of persons to whom the document
-- src:4191 | is to be served, or the business address, residential address
-- src:4192 | or last email address of the individual or body, cannot be
-- src:4193 | ascertained — by posting it on a website that is maintained
-- src:4194 | by the Authority and prescribed by the Minister by
-- src:4195 | notification in the Gazette for this purpose; or
-- src:4197 | (c) by any other method authorised by the regulations for the
-- src:4198 | service of documents of that kind if the addressee consents
-- src:4199 | (expressly or impliedly) to service of a document of that
-- src:4200 | kind in that way.
@ref s 64(2) to (5): the ways a document may be served, by kind of person (src:4115-4200)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
      w IS A `Way to serve a document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64 the document may be served in this way on this kind of person` MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `give it personally to the individual, or to a partner, secretary or other similar officer, or manager` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `leave it at, or send it by prepaid registered post to, the address the section names` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `leave it with an adult apparently resident or employed at the individual's address` THEN (k EQUALS `an individual`)
    WHEN `affix a copy in a conspicuous place at the individual's address` THEN (k EQUALS `an individual`)
    WHEN `send it by fax` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `send it by email` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `give an electronic notice by the addressee's chosen means of notification` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `post it on the website the Minister prescribed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `use another method the regulations authorise, with the addressee's consent` THEN TRUE

-- src:4189 | (b) where by the exercise of reasonable diligence, the name of
-- src:4190 | any individual or a body of persons to whom the document
-- src:4191 | is to be served, or the business address, residential address
-- src:4192 | or last email address of the individual or body, cannot be
-- src:4193 | ascertained — by posting it on a website that is maintained
-- src:4194 | by the Authority and prescribed by the Minister by
-- src:4195 | notification in the Gazette for this purpose; or
@ref s 64(5)(b) (src:4189-4195)
GIVEN `by the exercise of reasonable diligence the name of the individual or body of persons, or their business address, residential address or last email address, cannot be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(5)(b) the document may be served by posting it on the website the Authority maintains and the Minister prescribed` MEANS
    `by the exercise of reasonable diligence the name of the individual or body of persons, or their business address, residential address or last email address, cannot be ascertained`

-- src:4205 | (6) Service of a document under this section takes effect —
-- src:4207 | (a) if the document is sent by fax and a notification of
-- src:4208 | successful transmission is received — on the day of
-- src:4209 | transmission;
-- src:4211 | (b) if the document is sent by email — at the time that the
-- src:4212 | email becomes capable of being retrieved by the person to
-- src:4213 | whom it is sent;
-- src:4215 | (c) if the document is sent by prepaid registered post — 2 days
-- src:4216 | after the day the document was posted (even if it is returned
-- src:4217 | undelivered); or
-- src:4219 | (d) if the document is posted on a website mentioned in
-- src:4220 | subsection (5)(b) — at the beginning of the day after the
-- src:4221 | date on which subsection (5)(b) has been complied with.
@ref s 64(6)(a), (c) (src:4205-4221)
-- When service takes effect, on dates. By fax with successful transmission notice: the day of transmission. By prepaid registered post: 2 days after the day posted (even if returned undelivered).
-- By email: the time it becomes capable of being retrieved (a time, not a date: asked as the day). By website: the beginning of the day after the date (b) was complied with.
GIVEN w IS A `Way to serve a document`
      `the day of transmission, posting, retrieval or posting on the website` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 64(6) the day service takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `send it by fax` THEN JUST `the day of transmission, posting, retrieval or posting on the website`
    WHEN `send it by email` THEN JUST `the day of transmission, posting, retrieval or posting on the website`
    WHEN `leave it at, or send it by prepaid registered post to, the address the section names` THEN JUST (Date (Day `the day of transmission, posting, retrieval or posting on the website` PLUS 2))
    WHEN `post it on the website the Minister prescribed` THEN JUST (Date (Day `the day of transmission, posting, retrieval or posting on the website` PLUS 1))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4223 | (7) However, service of any document under this Act on a person by
-- src:4224 | email or by an electronic notice at the person’s chosen means of
-- src:4225 | notification, may be effected only with the person’s prior consent
-- src:4226 | (express or implied) to service in that way.
@ref s 64(7) (src:4223-4226)
GIVEN `the person has given prior consent, express or implied, to service by that means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(7) service by email or by an electronic notice may be effected` MEANS
    `the person has given prior consent, express or implied, to service by that means`

-- src:4228 | (8) This section does not apply to documents to be served in
-- src:4229 | proceedings in court.
@ref s 64(8) (src:4228-4229)
GIVEN `the document is to be served in proceedings in court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(8) section 64 applies to the document` MEANS
    NOT `the document is to be served in proceedings in court`

-- src:4231 | (9) In this section —
-- src:4233 | “Act” includes any subsidiary legislation made under this Act;
-- src:4235 | “business address” means —
-- src:4237 | (a) in the case of an individual, the individual’s usual or
-- src:4238 | last known place of business, or place of
-- src:4239 | employment, in Singapore; or
-- src:4241 | (b) in the case of a partnership (other than a limited
-- src:4242 | liability partnership), the partnership’s principal or
-- src:4243 | last known place of business in Singapore;
-- src:4245 | “chosen means of access”, for an addressee on whom is or is to
-- src:4246 | be served a document permitted or required by this Act,
-- src:4247 | means an electronic means the addressee agrees with the
-- src:4248 | person giving or serving the document as the means by which
-- src:4249 | the addressee may access that document’s contents;
-- src:4254 | “chosen means of notification”, for an addressee on whom is or
-- src:4255 | is to be served a document permitted or required by this Act,
-- src:4256 | means an electronic means that the addressee nominates to
-- src:4257 | the person giving or serving the document as the means by
-- src:4258 | which the addressee may be notified that such a document
-- src:4259 | has been served on the addressee;
-- src:4261 | “document” includes a notice permitted or required by this Act
-- src:4262 | to be served;
-- src:4264 | “last email address” means the last email address given by the
-- src:4265 | addressee concerned to the person giving or serving the
-- src:4266 | document as the email address for the service of documents
-- src:4267 | under this Act;
-- src:4269 | “residential address” means an individual’s usual or last known
-- src:4270 | place of residence in Singapore.
@ref s 64(9) definitions (src:4231-4270)
GIVEN `it is subsidiary legislation made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) Act includes this subsidiary legislation` MEANS
    IF `it is subsidiary legislation made under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4235 | “business address” means —
-- src:4237 | (a) in the case of an individual, the individual’s usual or
-- src:4238 | last known place of business, or place of
-- src:4239 | employment, in Singapore; or
-- src:4241 | (b) in the case of a partnership (other than a limited
-- src:4242 | liability partnership), the partnership’s principal or
-- src:4243 | last known place of business in Singapore;
@ref s 64(9) "business address" (src:4235-4243)
GIVEN `it is an individual's usual or last known place of business, or place of employment, in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a partnership's principal or last known place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) the place is a business address` MEANS
    `it is an individual's usual or last known place of business, or place of employment, in Singapore` OR `it is a partnership's principal or last known place of business in Singapore`

-- src:4245 | “chosen means of access”, for an addressee on whom is or is to
-- src:4246 | be served a document permitted or required by this Act,
-- src:4247 | means an electronic means the addressee agrees with the
-- src:4248 | person giving or serving the document as the means by which
-- src:4249 | the addressee may access that document’s contents;
@ref s 64(9) "chosen means of access" (src:4245-4249)
GIVEN `it is an electronic means the addressee agrees with the person serving as the means to access the document's contents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) the means is the chosen means of access` MEANS
    `it is an electronic means the addressee agrees with the person serving as the means to access the document's contents`

-- src:4254 | “chosen means of notification”, for an addressee on whom is or
-- src:4255 | is to be served a document permitted or required by this Act,
-- src:4256 | means an electronic means that the addressee nominates to
-- src:4257 | the person giving or serving the document as the means by
-- src:4258 | which the addressee may be notified that such a document
-- src:4259 | has been served on the addressee;
@ref s 64(9) "chosen means of notification" (src:4254-4259)
GIVEN `it is an electronic means the addressee nominates as the means to be notified that a document has been served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) the means is the chosen means of notification` MEANS
    `it is an electronic means the addressee nominates as the means to be notified that a document has been served`

-- src:4261 | “document” includes a notice permitted or required by this Act
-- src:4262 | to be served;
@ref s 64(9) "document" (src:4261-4262)
GIVEN `it is a notice permitted or required by this Act to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) document includes this notice` MEANS
    IF `it is a notice permitted or required by this Act to be served` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4264 | “last email address” means the last email address given by the
-- src:4265 | addressee concerned to the person giving or serving the
-- src:4266 | document as the email address for the service of documents
-- src:4267 | under this Act;
@ref s 64(9) "last email address" (src:4264-4267)
GIVEN `it is the last email address the addressee gave the person serving as the address for service of documents under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) the address is the last email address` MEANS
    `it is the last email address the addressee gave the person serving as the address for service of documents under this Act`

-- src:4269 | “residential address” means an individual’s usual or last known
-- src:4270 | place of residence in Singapore.
@ref s 64(9) "residential address" (src:4269-4270)
GIVEN `it is an individual's usual or last known place of residence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 64(9) the place is a residential address` MEANS
    `it is an individual's usual or last known place of residence in Singapore`

§ `64A. Financial penalties, etc., payable to Consolidated Fund`

-- src:4276 | 64A. All fines imposed under section 12(1) and all financial
-- src:4277 | penalties ordered under section 45N(1) —
-- src:4279 | (a) may be recovered by the Authority in any court of
-- src:4280 | competent jurisdiction as if they were simple contract
-- src:4281 | debts; and
-- src:4283 | (b) must be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 64A (src:4276-4283)
GIVEN `it is a fine imposed under section 12(1) or a financial penalty ordered under section 45N(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64A the fine or penalty may be recovered by the Authority in a court as if it were a simple contract debt and must be paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `it is a fine imposed under section 12(1) or a financial penalty ordered under section 45N(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `65. Amendment of First, Second and Third Schedules`

-- src:4289 | 65.—(1) The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, at any
-- src:4290 | time amend the First, Second or Third Schedule.
@ref s 65(1) (src:4289-4290)
GIVEN `the Minister has amended the Schedule by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(1) the Schedule reads as amended` MEANS
    `the Minister has amended the Schedule by notification in the Gazette`

-- src:4292 | (2) The Minister may, in any notification made under
-- src:4293 | subsection (1), make such incidental, consequential or
-- src:4294 | supplementary provisions as may be necessary or expedient.
@ref s 65(2) (src:4292-4294)
GIVEN `the notification contains incidental, consequential or supplementary provisions necessary or expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 65(2) the notification may contain those provisions` MEANS
    `the notification contains incidental, consequential or supplementary provisions necessary or expedient`

§ `66. Regulations`

-- src:4298 | 66. The Authority may, with the approval of the Minister, make
-- src:4299 | regulations —
-- src:4304 | (a) required or permitted to be prescribed by this Act; and
-- src:4306 | (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or
-- src:4307 | giving effect to the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 66 (src:4298-4307)
GIVEN `the Authority has made the regulations with the approval of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are required or permitted to be prescribed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66 the regulations are validly made under the section` MEANS
    `the Authority has made the regulations with the approval of the Minister` AND (`they are required or permitted to be prescribed by this Act` OR `they are necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to the purposes of this Act`)

§ `68. Transitional and saving provisions`

-- src:4313 | 68.—(1) All acts done by the Singapore Broadcasting Authority
-- src:4314 | before 1 January 2003 continue to remain valid and applicable as
-- src:4315 | though done by the Authority, until the time invalidated, revoked,
-- src:4316 | cancelled or otherwise determined by the Authority.
@ref s 68(1) (src:4313-4316)
GIVEN `the act was done by the Singapore Broadcasting Authority before 1 January 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been invalidated, revoked, cancelled or otherwise determined by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(1) the act continues valid and applicable as though done by the Authority` MEANS
    `the act was done by the Singapore Broadcasting Authority before 1 January 2003` AND (NOT `it has been invalidated, revoked, cancelled or otherwise determined by the Authority`)

-- src:4318 | (2) Any decision, document, licence, consent, approval or
-- src:4319 | authorisation prepared, made, issued or granted by the Singapore
-- src:4320 | Broadcasting Authority under the Singapore Broadcasting Authority
-- src:4321 | Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition) before 1 January 2003 is, so far
-- src:4322 | as it is not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act, deemed to be a
-- src:4323 | decision, document, licence, consent, approval or authorisation
-- src:4324 | prepared, made, issued or granted by the Authority.
@ref s 68(2) (src:4318-4324)
GIVEN `it is a decision, document, licence, consent, approval or authorisation made, issued or granted by the Singapore Broadcasting Authority under the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition) before 1 January 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(2) it is deemed to have been made, issued or granted by the Authority` MEANS
    `it is a decision, document, licence, consent, approval or authorisation made, issued or granted by the Singapore Broadcasting Authority under the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition) before 1 January 2003` AND (NOT `it is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act`)

-- src:4326 | (3) Where anything has been commenced by or on behalf of the
-- src:4327 | Singapore Broadcasting Authority before 1 January 2003, the thing
-- src:4328 | may be carried on and completed by or under the authority of the
-- src:4329 | Authority.
@ref s 68(3) (src:4326-4329)
GIVEN `the thing was commenced by or on behalf of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority before 1 January 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(3) the thing may be carried on and completed by or under the authority of the Authority` MEANS
    `the thing was commenced by or on behalf of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority before 1 January 2003`

-- src:4331 | (4) Despite the repeal of Part XI of the Singapore Broadcasting
-- src:4332 | Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition), as from 1 January
-- src:4333 | 2003, sections 49 to 53 of that Act continue in force and to apply to
-- src:4334 | the broadcasting successor companies mentioned in those sections as
-- src:4335 | if that Part has not been repealed.
@ref s 68(4) (src:4331-4335)
GIVEN `it is a broadcasting successor company mentioned in sections 49 to 53 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(4) sections 49 to 53 of that Act continue in force and apply to the company as if Part XI had not been repealed` MEANS
    `it is a broadcasting successor company mentioned in sections 49 to 53 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition)`

-- src:4337 | (5) In this section, “broadcasting successor companies” means
-- src:4338 | companies nominated by the Minister for the purposes of the repealed
-- src:4339 | section 49 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297,
-- src:4340 | 1995 Revised Edition).
@ref s 68(5) (src:4337-4340)
GIVEN `it is a company nominated by the Minister for the purposes of the repealed section 49 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(5) the company is a broadcasting successor company` MEANS
    `it is a company nominated by the Minister for the purposes of the repealed section 49 of the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297, 1995 Revised Edition)`
